      "content": "It's important to remember that Tylenol helps with pain relief but is not a substitute for rest and proper recovery. Typically, it is recommended to not exceed 3,000 mg (3 tablets, as each tablet typically contains 325 mg of acetaminophen) in a 24-hour period unless advised by a healthcare professional. Consider gentle stretching, cooling baths, and taking short naps to aid your recovery. Ensure you stay hydrated and eat a balanced diet to replenish your body’s nutrients. It's crucial not to over-rely on any medication and to always consult with a healthcare professional if needed.",
